.TH COMMONANCESTOR 1
.SH NAME
commonancestor \- a binary search tree, and four lines of search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/commonancestor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I CommonAncestor
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/CommonAncestor.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Thirty-two random keys inserted one every fifty milliseconds, so the tree
grows while you watch, with duplicates dropped.  The last two inserted
are the pair whose lowest common ancestor is wanted; they are red, and
the ancestor is green, or yellow if it is one of them.
.PP
The search needs no parent pointers and no second pass: descend from the
root, and the first node the two keys fall on opposite sides of \- or that
is one of them \- is the answer, because a search tree has already sorted
them.  The drawing is an in-order walk carrying one x cursor down the
recursion, so a node lands one column right of its whole left subtree and
nothing ever overlaps.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B left / right
Scroll
.TP
.B "any other key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/commonancestor.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
